<title>JAPAN: Victor Co shares climb to 1997 high.</title>
<headline>Victor Co shares climb to 1997 high.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Victor Co of Japan Ltd, a leading manufacturer of video cassette recorders, rose to a new high for the calendar year on Monday morning.</p>
<p>The shares were supported by news earlier this month that the firm plans to start selling digital video cassette recorders in October, traders said.</p>
<p>At 0152 GMT, the share price was up 40 yen at 1,600. It earlier hit a 1997 high of 1,610. Volume was 1.546 million shares.</p>
